  "description": "EGIJOT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C140 H310 Cl11 Na1 Nd12 O28,2(C4 H10 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 5 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 3 O neighbors; Nd9 (Nd) has 3 O neighbors; Nd10 (Nd) has 3 O neighbors; Nd11 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors; Nd12 (Nd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.719-3.903 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.99-106.70°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd12(OtAm)26(HOtAm)2Cl11Na]·2Et2O.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
